1. setup a virtual environment
python -m venv myenv

2. activate virtual env
source venv/bin/activate

3. install pytorch with cuda 12.1
pip3 install torch torchvision torchaudio --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121

4. setup pycharm
    Open PyCharm.
    Open your project or create a new one.
    Go to File > Settings (Windows) or PyCharm > Preferences (Mac).
    In the settings window, navigate to Project: [your project name] > Python Interpreter.
    Click the gear icon and select Add.
    In the dialog that appears, choose Existing environment and select the Python executable from the virtual environment:
        For Windows, navigate to myenv\Scripts\python.exe.
        For Mac/Linux, navigate to myenv/bin/python.
    Click OK to save the changes and select the virtual environment as the interpreter.

